# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored — never commit it.
# Read by scripts/factory-secrets.sh, which copies these values out into
# every new project's own GitHub Actions secrets — this file isn't
# ai-app-factory's own config so much as a personal, reusable staging area
# for provisioning *other* repos. See DESIGN.md's "GH_PAT: token strategy"
# and docs/adr/0001-design-to-issues-loop.md for the full picture.

# From `claude setup-token` (Claude Code OAuth, not an API key — see
# README.md's Setup section for why: this authenticates against your Claude
# subscription, not pay-per-token billing). Copied verbatim into every new
# project's own CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN secret.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=

# A fine-grained GitHub PAT scoped to "All repositories" with `Contents`,
# `Issues`, `Pull requests`, `Actions`, `Secrets` (Read and write) — not
# `Administration`, not `Workflows`.
#
# CORRECTED 2026-08-17 — this was originally (wrongly) scoped to just
# `Secrets: Read and write`, on the reasoning that factory-secrets.sh only
# calls `gh secret set`. True, but irrelevant: that call authenticates with
# your *local* `gh` login, not this value. This value is the payload that
# gets written into every new project's own GH_PAT secret, and THAT repo's
# claude.yml/seed-milestones.yml then use it for real Contents/Issues/PRs/
# Actions work. A Secrets-only token broke the very first real seeding run
# (could create issues, 403'd on every milestone/label/comment/edit).
#
# "All repositories" is still unavoidable (this value seeds a repo that
# doesn't exist yet, same reasoning ai-app-factory's own GH_PAT no longer
# needs to deal with post-redesign) — but capability is otherwise identical
# to what a single generated repo's own token needs, nothing broader.
GH_PAT=
